VCU1000 GUI design notes

Setup screen:

  4 fields which are pure readback
  3 data entry/feedback
  1 button (reset)
  - Should communicate that this might cause data loss - e.g. make red, put 
    somewhere it won't be clicked accidentally.
  - Maybe also change the name - reset sounds like it might simply restore
    defaults (which actually the real command won't do). Perhaps "Power cycle" 
    or something similar?
  
Main screen:

  Status at top - most prominent piece of information
  
  Pressure grouped with voltage.
  - Current pressure, with setpoint & tolerance.
  - Current voltage, with setpoint & percentage.
  - Reg. Timeout
  
  Timer control in separate visual group.
  
  2 main button toggles:
  - Remote mode
  - Regulation

  2 window-level buttons:
  - Configuration
  - Exit
  
  
Design 1 notes:

- Remote mode readback is separated from control
- Timeout is a headache - only means anything if reg. is on, but is not grouped
  with reg. control. 
- In Error mode, won't be obvious how to recover - either set regulation off
  or use reset, but reset is on config panel and reg will already be reading as
  off.
  - Though actually, set regulation on will work fine as well - will restart reg.
- Not very obvious that pressure SP is only meaningful if we want closed loop 
  control, while voltage SP only does anything in open-loop.
  
Design 2:

- Regroup controls - separate into groups:
                      * Readback
                      * Closed loop (or regulated/automatic)
                      * Open loop   (or manual)
                      
                      
                      
Abstract away raw access to regulation On/Off. Instead have top level control:
- Control mode <Manual|Regulated>

- Readback just contains RBV for pressure, voltage and percentage.
- Manual control just contains voltage SP.
- Regulated control contains:
  - Pressure SP
  - Pressure tolerance
  - Regulation Start/Stop toggle
  - Reg timeout
  - Time toggle On/Off
  - Timer setting/readback
  
Use internal database logic to implement abstracted control mode and interlocks,
and use Invalid alarm severity on disabled output records to communicate effects
of toggle (DISV field should be used for this - shouldn't just be alarm, or else
will find control turns white but writes to the field still work). 

Should also abstract the Status field - if in Regulated mode, should just report
raw GET Status value, but if in Manual mode should report either just "manual control"
or else "Pressure on target" or "Pressure off target" depending on whether we want
to pay any regard to the pressure setpoint/tolerance in manual mode. 

Note with this grouping it would be very nice if we could implement our own 
timeout counter in the DB, since the timeout field is confusingly grouped 
together with the timer controls. An explicit readback of the timer countdown
would make this distinction more intuitive. This does trade off correctness for
usability - we open ourselves to possibility our timeout count could become 
inaccurate as device state changes before we can update the database.

Note in either case we abstract away the TimerTarget readback - should be OK 
to only ever report the CurrentTimer value. Difference between values only 
ever becomes relevant if RESET function is used. If user is setting it, it should
always reset the current timer - which we want anyway. If reg ends because timer 
expires, it may make sense to reset it to original value ready for next sample, 
but this would need implementing in DB anyway since it is not what the device 
does. 

Testing notes/bug list:

- Pressure displays with right mantissa but wrong exponent, i.e. shows 9.90000
when true value is 9.9e-03. 
  Fixed - set to use exp notation rather than default.
- Voltage percentage is actually a ratio between 0 and 1, not 0 and 100.
- Seems to be a lag in reporting of timer count - doesn't count down steadily.
- Same effect for other fast monitored values i.e. voltage and pressure.
- Text entry fields don't show current value of setpoint - default to e.g. 0.0
for pressure, which is confusing since hitting "Regulation On" immediately will 
not cause to home towards 0.0. Possibly this is a db error - db is initialised 
with different setpoints from the device, and EDM reflects these defaults - text
update fields do display current setpoint if e.g. it is changed by an external caput. 
- Text entry fields permit setting variable to invalid values, and wrongly appear
to report success - e.g. can set pressure setpoint to -1.0.
  Fixed by setting the "Clip to HOPR/LOPR" checkbox. 
- Remote mode definitely confusing - not obvious device needs setting to Remote 
before changing values, as changing values seems to work immediately (error 
messages are staying in the IOC, not being reported at top level).
- Status record needs an alarms status. 
- Remote button is too narrow, text truncated. 
- Version string is truncated even further by configuration screen. Pertinent 
info is still there but is ugly as sin.
- Check precisions are sensible, and decide on a convention for units - either:
Pressure (mbar)   [6.0e-04     ]
or:
Pressure          [6.0e-04 mbar] 
- Try to fit full word "Tolerance" in PTOL field. 
- Set KP and KI to use exp notation?

- Voltage bug - sometimes manual voltage set won't work (field remains at zero).
  No message sent to device, no change in DB. 
  Only seems to occur if:
   - Not connected to this IOC before from EDM
  So can fix by:
   - Setting Edit then back to Execute
   - Closing EDM and reconnecting
   - Closing the window and reopening.

- Fix banner colour on setup window.
  * Done
  
- RBVs for Timer & Regulation buttons (as can end up in error state).
- Input range on TimerTarget (at least lower bound)
- Alarm status on CurrentTimer RBV, to indicate will do odd things when restarted.
  Options:
   - Set alarm state when we read back negative value 
   - Use database logic to try to anticipate the fault and set the alarm state 
