How bad is the congestion?
REM -    2s
STATUS - 1s
P      - 1s
P:TOL  - 2s
P:SP   - 2s
V      - 1s
V:PER  - 1s
V:MAX  - 2s
T:STA  - 1s
T      - 1s
T:TAR  - 1s
REG:STA- 1s
REG:TIM- 1s
REG:KI - 2s
REG:KP - 2s

So 12 updates per second (counting each 2s update as 0.5Hz).
Options:
 - Could make V:PER pure in-database calculation. No real advantage to reading
 direct from device, and eliminates a whole fast update record.
 - Drop REG:TIM and T:TAR to 2s? Shaves off another update/s.
 - Drop REG:KI & REG:KP to 5s? Gets us another 3/5 of an update/s.
 
 So down to 9.4 updates/s.
 
Still not enough to solve problem - going to try using PHAS field on records to 
ensure fast-changing fields are read with higher priority.
- That helped a bit - still a little laggy but no longer actually missing updates.

